comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T04:06:08.272Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete strict reads covered all 299 open items and zero in-progress items; all-status search recovered closed pm-lwmstb for post-merge routing, pm-baksix for pending receipt health, and pm-z1z96w for exact hash-only reconciliation. Their live resolutions do not own the newly proven machine-executable no-op remediation boundary. GitHub #1150 is therefore a distinct recurrence under the canonical concurrency lineage, not a duplicate."
  "2026-08-29T04:25:35.547Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: the linked registry plus temporary-repository suite passed 26/26. Manual acceptance in a fresh Git repository produced merge_receipts_pending and history_drift_merge_receipt, both mapped to pm merge reconcile; dry-run left strict health red and apply cleared it. The complete suite passed 586 files and 8,108 tests with exact 60,136/45,340/12,504/57,907 coverage at 100/100/100/100. Repository assurance, contracts, SDK/package parity, docstrings, defect evidence, graph and record gates passed; direct static reached only the known local RSS ratchet also reproduced on unchanged dependencies, while the prior exact hosted head passed that gate. ESLint, both zero-clone profiles, packed 13-package npx smoke, and fresh Bun/bunx tarball smoke passed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T04:25:35.098Z","harness:codex","Machine-executable remediation fields must name an operation whose successful completion changes the reported state. Preview commands belong in summaries and workflows, not as the only executable fix for a red gate."
